{"agent":"fleet-green-a","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The new `gate record` runs against `repo`, while the surrounding T1 work is done in `tree`. In this fixture `tree` is the worktree checked out on branch `T1` (`_git(tree, \"add\"/\"commit\")`, and the adjacent `run_cli(tree, \"gate\", \"run\", \"T1\", \"unit_tests\")`), and `repo` is the main checkout that the branch gets merged into (`run_cli(repo, \"merge\", \"T1\", \"--allow-dirty\")`). So the call records `implement` while the cwd is on main, not on the branch that the comment right below/above says must be \"still ahead of main\". If `gate record` binds the evidence to the current checkout/commit, the implement evidence is attached to main's pre-merge commit instead of T1's commit; after `merge T1` advances main, that evidence no longer certifies the commit it was meant to, so either the assertion that the untracked file (left in `tree`) does not make the evidence stale passes for the wrong reason, or the implement evidence is reported stale after the merge and the fix does not actually make the test pass. The same instruction issued in `tree` (where the branch under test is checked out) would bind to T1 and match the comment's intent.","digest":"3575aa65eeba15c0","location":"tests/test_stale_after_merge.py:318","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_stale_after_merge.py:318"}],"chunks_total":1,"combined_gates":["rubber_duck","critic"],"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":957,"diff_sha":"ced51a7f75155b192e1926d94ddf4c8baff65be3ba6ca5c1217a363a266377ce","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":118.0,"family":"deepseek","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","output_digest":"2bf7d714ba5e1b90","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B658d70677d.rubber_duck.lan-de